      },
      {
        "source": "README.md:80",
        "text": "lol  `\u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af`. Not bad for a character-level model after 3 minutes of training on a GPU. Better results are quite likely obtainable by instead finetuning a pretrained GPT-2 model on this dataset (s"
      },
      {
        "source": "README.md:88",
        "text": "Here, since we are running on CPU instead of GPU we must set both `--device=cpu` and also turn off PyTorch 2.0 compile with `--compile=False`. Then when we evaluate we get a bit more noisy but faster "
      },
      {
        "source": "README.md:105",
